WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.430
- I just ordered six different burgers,

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:05.460
five of them being vegetarian,
one of them being beef.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.750
Will I taste a difference?

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:07.920
Which one will I like better?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.280
Are vegetarian burgers actually healthy?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.113
(doorbell dings)

00:00:11.113 --> 00:00:12.740
(door clunks)

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.860
- Enjoy your burgers.

00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:16.143
(door thuds)

00:00:16.143 --> 00:00:21.143
(easy going intense bass
beats and digital music)

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.370
- I'm coming fresh off my
30 day vegan challenge.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.260
I hope you enjoyed watching it last week.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.030
During my 30 day vegan trial,

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.050
I actually ate some vegan burgers.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:31.820
And since they're all the rage,

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.530
I decided to put them to the test.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.040
I want to focus on three things here,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.470
looking at all the nutrition facts.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.440
First, calories,
Impossible Burger rings in

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.160
as the most calorie dense, 710 calories,

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.310
when compared to 630
for the Beyond Burger,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.560
650 for a regular burger.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.830
And the lowest being the
quinoa at 510 calories.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.360
Next, I want to jump
to the sodium content.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.690
I didn't expect this.

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:58.200
But the meatless burgers actually have

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.890
really high sodium contents,

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:01.880
more than the actual beef burger!

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.850
The beef burger has 780
milligrams of sodium.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.920
But the Beyond patty has 950,

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.850
and the Impossible has 1,210!

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.880
Even the quinoa has 730.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:12.930
It's clear that these meatless burgers

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.650
are trying to up the flavor
by putting more salt in there.

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:17.420
Which can be problematic
for those who have

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.260
high blood pressure, or heart disease.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.960
That can put a lot of strain on the heart.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:24.130
And the final macronutrient
I want focus on is protein.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.880
I would think the beef burger would have

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.080
the highest amount of
protein, but that's not true.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.390
Impossible Burger, 47 grams of protein

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.920
compared to the beef, 39 grams,

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.530
compared to the Beyond Burger, 33 grams.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.710
And then the rest of
these, the black bean,

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.870
sweet potato and quinoa
are in the low 20s.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.000
Why is that important?

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.670
Well, first of all you need
protein to sustain muscle,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.050
especially for myself,
'cause you know I'm trying

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.030
to be a muscular person. (growls)

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.600
But also because you need
protein to feel satiated,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.700
meaning to feel full.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.610
Having the Impossible Burger
have 47 grams of protein

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:59.130
will mean that you'll eat it
and probably feel very full.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.970
As opposed to a sweet potato burger,

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.510
only 20 grams of protein,

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.990
you still may be hungry
after eating that one.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.680
I'm ready to try these burgers.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.220
I want to know what they
feel like on my tongue,

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.400
what they smell like,
what they taste like.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.230
And, for you to get my rating.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.620
All right, it's time to
blindfold myself with a tie.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.690
Gray what?

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:18.670
Christian who?

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:20.820
I'm ready for my first burger.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:21.710
- [Staff Member] Give
them a little shuffle,

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:22.790
because he saw the stack.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:23.810
- I didn't see the stack.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.540
Why does everyone denying the fact

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.129
that I'm an honest human being.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:29.210
(plate scrapes)

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.890
I'm gonna talk about three
things on each of these burgers.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:35.300
One is the scent, the mouth feel,

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.272
as I like to call it the
mouthiness, and then taste.

00:02:37.272 --> 00:02:40.910
And then I'll give it a,
out of five stars, I guess.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.087
I feel like that's reasonable.

00:02:42.087 --> 00:02:43.368
(light, amusing music)

00:02:43.368 --> 00:02:47.630
(sighs) Oo, that warm brioche bun.

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.355
All of them have the same
ingredients, by the way.

00:02:50.355 --> 00:02:54.070
(breathes in) Scent-wise I
already smell vegetables.

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:55.840
It almost smells like a sweet potato,

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:58.344
but I don't want to judge
it just yet, all right.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.840
(food crunches)

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.720
Oh, no I know which one this is.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.381
This is the bean one for sure.

00:03:05.381 --> 00:03:06.790
Is this ever gonna trick anyone

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.087
to say that they're eating meat?

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.022
(lettuce crunches)

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:09.927
Wow, big piece of lettuce.

00:03:09.927 --> 00:03:11.610
Do I have thing in my teeth?

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.830
Mouthiness, I would say,

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.700
I could mouth and feel the
bean, which is kind of weird.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:19.370
It doesn't taste like a regular burger.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:20.840
The fact that it has standard ingredients

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.530
like lettuce, and tomato and
cheese makes it taste better.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:26.250
But it has a little
bit of sweetness to it.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.090
And that taste, right away
you get the bean thing

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.080
hitting you right in the face,

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.080
like you're eating a Chipotle
burrito or something.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.280
I'll probably give this two out of five.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.227
Sorry bean burger.

00:03:35.227 --> 00:03:36.190
(plate scrapes)
Next.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.351
Time to hydrate. (lips smacking)

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:41.717
(amusing acoustic
orchestral strings music)

00:03:41.717 --> 00:03:43.700
(plate scrapes)

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:46.013
Okay, this one smells decent.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.880
Oh my god, this could be, this could be,

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.287
this could be beef.

00:03:52.287 --> 00:03:54.380
(sighs) It smells really good.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.910
I really feel like this is beef.

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.582
Let's give it a taste.

00:03:57.582 --> 00:03:58.752
(food crunches)

00:03:58.752 --> 00:04:02.580
(amusing, plucking acoustic
orchestral strings music)

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:05.880
See I think this one's trying
to be beef really hard.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.920
I'm still getting a
little vegetable-y kick.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:08.933
This is really good.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:13.370
There's something about it

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.490
that I'm not buying that it's meat.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:18.010
There's just something,
there's like a little,

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.860
mouthfeel is really good,
though, really good.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:21.800
Tastes like beef.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.070
It falls apart like
beef, it could be beef,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.020
but I don't think so.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.410
I'm' gonna go ahead and guess this is

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.610
the Impossible Burger.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.610
This one gets three out
of five stars from me.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.443
Next!

00:04:30.443 --> 00:04:31.560
Cleansing the pallette!

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.701
Why am I yelling?

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:33.534
(hiccups)

00:04:33.534 --> 00:04:34.800
(skin rustling) All right.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.630
Burger numero tres.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:39.800
Oh this one's heavy. (chuckles)

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.140
Oh yeah!

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:44.700
This feels, this is a beef patty.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:45.950
If I'm getting tricked on this,

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.420
it's a really embarrassing bit.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.374
It smells like a fresh burger.

00:04:49.374 --> 00:04:51.270
(food crunches)

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.310
Yeah, this is a beef burger.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.770
My protein sensors on my
tongue are lighting up.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.370
If it's not, I swear to god it's crazy.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.400
That tastes like beef,
it smells like beef,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.050
the consistency is like beef.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:04.030
It's not a great burger.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:06.630
I'll give it like a
four out of five, next.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:07.652
But that was the burger, right?

00:05:07.652 --> 00:05:08.707
(wrappers crinkling)

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:09.650
- [Staff Member] No.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:10.641
- No?!

00:05:10.641 --> 00:05:11.474
Are you not gonna tell me?

00:05:11.474 --> 00:05:14.620
All right, burgero numero quatro.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.352
Oh my god, this tastes like,

00:05:16.352 --> 00:05:18.930
to me it smells like pure vegetable.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.401
God now I'm confused, is
it a vegetable burger?

00:05:21.401 --> 00:05:22.800
(food crunches)

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.628
I don't know what this one is doing.

00:05:24.628 --> 00:05:26.070
You know what's funny?

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.680
I don't ask for sauce on any of these,

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.170
and this one has sauce, so it's confusing.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.470
I have no idea.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:34.960
What do we have left, Beyond, quinoa.

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.540
This might be the Beyond Burger.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.290
It smells kind of like meat.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:39.680
I think this is a Beyond Burger.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.200
I think the consistency is
pretty consistent with meat.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.200
I want to just take a bite of the patty.

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.430
It's really close to beef.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.410
It's like beef, but a little bit sweeter.

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:51.250
I'll give it three out of five stars.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.710
All right, (sighs) numero cinco.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.440
(amusing syncopated music)

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:56.573
Solid weight.

00:05:57.816 --> 00:05:59.246
It has no real scent.

00:05:59.246 --> 00:06:01.790
(food crunches)

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:03.010
Again with the sauce.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:04.560
Oh my god, what is that?

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:06.960
Is this the Beyond or Impossible burger?

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.860
That's good!

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.753
Oh my god, this might
be the Beyond Burger.

00:06:09.753 --> 00:06:11.302
It's definitely not meat.

00:06:11.302 --> 00:06:13.370
(laughs) If it's meat I'm so embarrassed.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.513
I messed up one of the other ones.

00:06:14.513 --> 00:06:16.450
This is either Impossible or Beyond.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.270
Or is this quinoa, god.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.073
The taste is weird, it's a weird taste.

00:06:22.073 --> 00:06:22.906
(food crunches)

00:06:22.906 --> 00:06:25.540
I don't like this taste,
I give it two stars.

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:26.900
I don't know what that is.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:27.860
We're gonna mark the fifth one

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.757
as a question mark for now, next?

00:06:28.757 --> 00:06:30.180
- [Staff Member] Didn't you just say

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.700
it was really good?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.970
- Like really good in tricking
you with the mouth feel.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.326
Saved the best for last.

00:06:36.326 --> 00:06:39.050
Oh, this one's got some weight to it.

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:42.210
Okay, this is definitely
one of the vegetarian ones.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:43.550
God, I'm getting a little nauseous.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:44.780
This is a quinoa burger.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.080
I just got like a huge hit of quinoa.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.170
Or no!

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.656
Sorry, sweet potato.

00:06:49.656 --> 00:06:51.005
(food crunches)

00:06:51.005 --> 00:06:53.570
(amusing, syncopated
acoustic orchestral strings)

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.790
Mouth feel, really bad.

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.660
It tastes like you're eating
a sweet burger, it's not good.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:06:59.885
One star.

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:01.330
(plate scrapes)
Blech!

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.460
Okay, here's my list.
(pen clinks)

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:04.670
Let's see how I did here.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:07.310
Burger number one was a black bean burger.

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:10.620
I gave it two stars, and
I said it was black beans.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:11.600
Which is correct!

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:15.880
The second one was a
quinoa patty, I said beef?

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:17.220
I really said it was beef?

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:18.170
No I didn't.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.000
I gave it three stars,
wow the quinoa patty's

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.430
coming in here and surprising me.

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.040
Third was the beef patty, I knew that.

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.290
I gave it four stars.

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:26.990
Four was they Beyond Burger
and I got the Beyond Burger.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:27.823
What's up?!

00:07:27.823 --> 00:07:31.610
Five was Impossible and
I said, questionable,

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:33.510
Beyond, Impossible, or quinoa.

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:34.560
I couldn't get that one.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:36.710
And then the sweet potato
I said it was sweet potato

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:38.210
and I gave it one star.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.660
I did really good, I got five out of six.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:41.640
Come on, that's impressive!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:42.830
You guys got to give me some love

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:44.120
for getting five out of six.

00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:46.610
I think the biggest shocker
out of all of this is,

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.570
I said quinoa patty was questionably beef.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.400
I gave it three stars,
and I thought it was

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:52.590
an Impossible Burger.

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.160
I'm surprised the Impossible
Burger kind of let me down.

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:56.750
Let's talk nutrition and health

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:58.520
when it comes to these meatless burgers.

00:07:58.520 --> 00:08:01.000
First, and it's the thing
that surprised me the most,

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.870
on the burgers that
tasted very close to meat,

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.640
they actually had macros
that were quite similar,

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.380
if not worse than the actual beef burger.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:11.250
For example, the
Impossible Burger has more

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.960
saturated fat, more calories, more sodium

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.320
than a traditional beef burger.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:18.570
I can't really go ahead and
call these health foods,

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:20.350
because they're still indulgences.

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:23.230
We should treat them the same
way as we do regular burgers.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.230
That you should have
them only occasionally,

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.470
only as a treat.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.470
Because if we fall into
the category of thinking

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.620
these are health foods,

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.400
people are gonna start
eating them as part of

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.290
their regular diets,
and that's not healthy.

00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:34.560
I noticed a pattern.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.010
The closer they taste to meat,

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:38.410
the more likely they are to be unhealthy

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.820
in terms of their macros.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.550
When I say unhealthy, I mean high amounts

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:44.800
of saturated fats, high in
calories, high in sodium.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.770
Because if you look at the sweet potato,

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.940
the quinoa, the black bean,

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.910
those are generally lower
in sodium, lower in fats

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.400
in comparison to the
Impossible and Beyond Burger

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.810
which tastes very, very similar
to the actual beef burger.

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:00.610
I think the biggest positive
of this meatless burgers

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.920
is that we can decrease
overall meat consumption.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.730
That's a good thing, not
only for your health,

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.410
but for the environment, as well.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.270
I'm a big fan of meatless Mondays.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.310
No one's saying you have to go vegan

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.330
in order to be healthy.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.340
You can decrease your meat consumption,

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:18.120
have a plant-focused diet and
still be incredibly healthy

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:19.920
if not healthier, than
if you were following

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.310
a traditional vegan diet.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.050
I actually said that in my vegan video.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.060
This is becoming a mega business.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:26.820
And I'm gonna keep a close eye on this,

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.580
just to make sure that we still
head in the right direction

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.160
and we don't start throwing
a bunch of preservatives,

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:34.540
and processed ingredients
into these meatless burgers.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.130
'Cause if something is to change,

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.970
I want to be the first
to let you guys know.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.730
Click here for my 30 day
vegan challenge video,

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.530
so you can see how I
suffered, where I improved,

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:45.050
